+//   of those resolutions found the texture the view already had ("race cost": same base 294,315 / 297,178 / 301,432 against replaced 1 / 3 / 30 in the windows 1200-1800),
+//   an estimated 2.3 to 8.6 M instructions a frame of the submit thread. A view depended on two process-wide counts: the serial tables' generation (g_ser_gen), which every
+//   texture made or finalized moves, and the write-tracking generation (nvn_dirty_now), which every guest write to a protected page moves, and both moved every frame.
+//   The rule here asks what moved, for which serial and in which pool:
+//   - the tables (rb_vs_moves): nothing; only serials no table held were added (patch 0073's count); moves noted for other serials (patch 0163's buckets; with this patch
