+//   submit thread, and, block-compressed, only with nothing on record to copy into it from a GPU-written texture over its storage. Never kept: an unclassified move, a
+//   move in its own bucket, a written pool, a placement sparse view, a virtual (sparse) pool or a finalized one, a finalized texture object (its lookups keep its
+//   shared texture or its ring entry in use), a view last resolved off the submit thread (no upload and no look is made there: the submit thread's next use makes them)
